{
  "id": "ep001",
  "version": 3,
  "topic": "strange things your body does while you sleep",
  "title": "Your Body Paralyzes You Every Night 😳",
  "description": "Every night your body paralyzes you, washes your brain and makes you taller — and you never notice. Which one surprised you most?",
  "hashtags": [
    "#shorts",
    "#facts",
    "#sleep",
    "#humanbody",
    "#didyouknow",
    "#science"
  ],
  "loop": true,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Every night, your body paralyzes you, and that's not even the weirdest part.",
      "shots": [
        "sleep paralysis",
        "woman sleeping dark bedroom",
        "man lying still bed night"
      ],
      "tag": "SLEEP"
    },
    {
      "text": "While you dream, your brain switches off almost every muscle, so you don't act out your dreams.",
      "shots": [
        "sleeping face night",
        "dream surreal fantasy",
        "person sleeping bed"
      ],
      "tag": "REM SLEEP"
    },
    {
      "text": "It also gives itself a bath. Fluid flushes out the waste your brain made all day.",
      "shots": [
        "brain mri scan",
        "brain glowing animation",
        "blue liquid flow"
      ],
      "tag": "BRAIN"
    },
    {
      "text": "You wake up about a centimeter taller, because the discs in your spine refill overnight.",
      "shots": [
        "spine vertebrae",
        "skeleton anatomy",
        "woman waking up stretching"
      ],
      "tag": "SPINE"
    },
    {
      "text": "Your nose goes off duty. Smoke rarely wakes a sleeping person, which is why smoke alarms are so loud.",
      "shots": [
        "smoke room dark",
        "smoke detector",
        "firefighter smoke"
      ],
      "tag": "SENSES"
    },
    {
      "text": "And that falling jolt as you drift off? It's a hypnic jerk, a muscle twitch, not a fall.",
      "shots": [
        "falling down",
        "man wakes up suddenly",
        "falling through clouds"
      ],
      "tag": "HYPNIC JERK"
    },
    {
      "text": "So tonight, remember:",
      "shots": [
        "eyes closing"
      ],
      "tag": "SLEEP"
    }
  ],
